(a) Before operating a taxicab within the city, a driver shall:
(1) Possess a valid Class C Georgia driver's license;
(2) Be competent to operate a motor vehicle;
(3) Be familiar with the traffic laws and ordinances of the State of Georgia and City of Morrow;
(4) Provide authorization and any information necessary to enable the chief of police or his designee to investigate the driver's background, criminal history, and traffic record;
(5) Provide a current motor vehicle report (drivers history report) at the time of original application and at renewal time;
(6) Be of good character as determined by the aforesaid investigation; and
(7) Obtain a driver's permit issued by the city.
